<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Two fair dice, one red and one blue, are rolled and the two numbers are added to give a score.</p><p>You may find a grid helpful.</p><p>Give each probability exactly, as a fraction or an exact decimal.</p><p>(a) How many equally likely outcomes are there?</p><div><fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find <m>P(\text{score} = {3})</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/>  </div><p>(c) Find <m>P(\text{score greater than } {5})</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans3"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Each of the 6 outcomes of the red die goes with each of the <m>{6}</m> outcomes of the blue die, so there are <m>6 \times {6} = {36}</m> equally likely outcomes. The grid shows the score for each one; the scores equal to <m>{3}</m> are in brackets and shaded.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Red \ Blue</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">1</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">2</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">3</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">4</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">5</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">6</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">1</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><span style="background:#d9d9d9;padding:0 4px;">(<m>{3}</m>)</span></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{7}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">2</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><span style="background:#d9d9d9;padding:0 4px;">(<m>{3}</m>)</span></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{7}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">3</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{7}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{9}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">4</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{7}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{9}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">5</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{7}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{9}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{11}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">6</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{7}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{9}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{11}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{12}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/></row></tabular><p>(b) <m>{2}</m> of the <m>{36}</m> cells have score <m>{3}</m>, so <m>P(\text{score} = {3}) = \dfrac{{2}}{{36}} = {\frac{1}{18}}</m>. The <m>{11}</m> different scores are not equally likely: count cells, not scores.</p><p>(c) <m>{26}</m> cells have a score greater than <m>{5}</m> (the score <m>{5}</m> itself is left out), so <m>P(\text{score greater than } {5}) = \dfrac{{26}}{{36}} = {\frac{13}{18}}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>36</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{1}{18}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{13}{18}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>